outputs.L1:
The invention relates to a production station for use in producing at least one layered bed, in particular a plurality of layered beds, of a magnetocaloric material. The station comprises a framework and, arranged at the framework, further comprises:

—a material receptacle for receiving a particulate magnetocaloric material;

—a dosing plate having at least one intake opening adapted to receive a magnetocaloric material of one layer of the layered bed;

—at least one reservoir below the at least one intake opening, wherein the reservoir is adapted to receive the one or more layers of the particulate magnetocaloric material;

wherein the production station further comprises:

—a shutter plate arranged between the reservoir and the dosing plate, wherein the shutter plate is switchable through motion with respect to the dosing plate, and wherein the shutter plate is arranged and adapted to at least activate a filling mode, wherein, in the filling mode, the at least one reservoir is filled with particulate magnetocaloric material of the one layer of the layered bed by switching control of the shutter plate.

outputs.L2:
The invention concerns a manufacturing station intended for producing at least one layered bed, and particularly several layered beds, made of magnetocaloric material. The station includes a framework and, for placement on the framework, comprises:

- a material container configured to hold particulate magnetocaloric material;
- a dosing plate provided with at least one inlet opening designed to take in magnetocaloric material for one layer of the layered bed;
- at least one reservoir positioned beneath the at least one inlet opening, the reservoir being configured to receive one or more layers of the particulate magnetocaloric material.

The production station additionally includes a shutter plate located between the reservoir and the dosing plate. The shutter plate can be switched by moving it relative to the dosing plate, and it is positioned and configured to at least enable a filling mode. In this filling mode, the at least one reservoir is supplied with particulate magnetocaloric material forming one layer of the layered bed through controlled switching of the shutter plate.

counterfactuals.output:
1. **A production station for producing layered magnetocaloric beds**, comprising:

a receptacle configured to receive particulate magnetocaloric material;

a dosing plate arranged below the receptacle, the dosing plate comprising a plurality of intake openings through which the particulate magnetocaloric material is metered from the receptacle;

a plurality of reservoirs arranged to receive and collect particulate magnetocaloric material passing through the intake openings of the dosing plate, each reservoir being associated with at least one of the intake openings; and

a movable shutter plate arranged between the dosing plate and the reservoirs, the movable shutter plate being displaceable between at least a first position, in which passage of the particulate magnetocaloric material from the intake openings to the reservoirs is blocked, and a second position, in which passage of the particulate magnetocaloric material from the intake openings to the reservoirs is permitted,

wherein movement of the movable shutter plate controls dosing of the particulate magnetocaloric material into the reservoirs for forming layers of a magnetocaloric bed.
